plugin.description:
Carried items, worn gear, the inside of every bag and the keyring in one window. Identical items
stack with a count, flags show as small letters, and the game's own {invmon} tags keep it current.
Only the carried list is asked of the game (invdata); what you are wearing, what is inside your bags
and what is on the keyring are read from dinv's database, so they cost no commands (and your own
"You are using:" equipment display stays quiet). "Read from the game" on the Worn tab asks anyway. Click an item for its
actions (wear, remove, get, put in a bag, drop, examine) or for dinv's details on it.

@YWindow:@w
@Yinvwin@w                 - show / hide the window
@Yinvwin inv|worn|bags|keyring|all@w   - choose a tab        (all = everything loaded)
@Yinvwin load@w            - read the inside of every bag
@Yinvwin refresh | invwin empty@w
@Yinvwin help@w            - print this list in the main window (also the Help chip in the window)

@YFinding things:@w
@Yinvwin <text>@w          - SEARCH carried items, every loaded bag and the keyring for that text, e.g. "invwin aardwolf"
                         ("invwin clear" removes it)
@Yinvwin type:potion spell:lotus@w   - targeted search, any mix of: type:<kind> wear:<slot> spell:<text>
                         @Ylvl:10 | lvl:1-10 | lvl:1 lvl:10 | lvl:10+ | lvl:<=10   flag:<word> in:<inv|worn|keyring|bag>@w
                         plus plain words ("quoted phrases" allowed). Searches carried items, bags, keyring and worn gear.
@Yinvwin gear|use|containers|loot|portals|other|any@w   - choose a kind of item
@Yinvwin slot head|neck|fingers|weapon|held|...@w  - gear worn in that slot (second chip row under Gear)
@Yinvwin sort level|name|type@w

@YItems:@w
@Yinvwin print on|off@w - on: i / inventory print this plugin's stacked list (counts, flag letters, level, in the item's
                     own colours) in the main window and refresh the window. Off (the default): this plugin prints nothing
                     and leaves i to the game or the serials plugin; the window still reads the data that goes by.
@Yinvwin serials on|off@w - item serial numbers in that printed list (i serials shows them once)
@Yinvwin shorterflags@w - flags print as configured in Aardwolf; this switches to the shorter [KMGH] (and back)
@Yinvwin objflag <options>@w - hide flags in the shorter form: kept invis magic glow hum tempered cursed envenomed
                     weakened nolocate (or their letters K I M G H T C E W N); showplus marks items that lost a flag.
                     No options lists them with On/Off; "invwin objflag all" turns every option off.
@Yinvwin identify wish|cast 'spell'|lore|room@w  - how the window identifies items (no argument lists them;
                         lore needs a donation room or city area, "room" needs room 32611 (Hester))
@Yid <item>@w          - the identify box also opens as a card ("identify", "lore" and casting your identify spell work too);
                     the original text still prints. Only identifies you type yourself open it.
